BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c930ac473c9c7380@zcyber-gtm.local
DTSTAMP:20260720T160039Z
DTSTART:20260723T170000Z
DTEND:20260723T220000Z
SUMMARY:Chicago InfoSec Managers Workshop - Western Burbs (Lisle)
DESCRIPTION:<h1>​Leading Under Pressure</h1><h2>​How Stress\, Communication &amp\; Leadership Behaviors Shape Cybersecurity Team Performance</h2><p>​Cybersecurity leaders are expected to operate in high-pressure environments where constant escalation\, incident fatigue\, staffing strain\, and nonstop communication demands have become normalized.</p><p>​But stress does not stay isolated to individuals.<br>It spreads through teams.</p><p>​The way leaders communicate during pressure — especially after incidents\, mistakes\, or prolonged overload — directly shapes psychological safety\, team trust\, engagement\, and long-term performance.</p><p>​Leading Under Pressure is a highly interactive 4-hour workshop designed specifically for cybersecurity managers and team leaders who want to better understand:</p><ul><li><p>​how stress changes leadership behavior</p></li><li><p>​how communication impacts team performance</p></li><li><p>​how burnout silently propagates through organizations</p></li><li><p>​how to build healthier\, more sustainable cybersecurity teams</p></li></ul><p>​This is not traditional leadership training.<br>It is a practical\, psychologically intelligent operational leadership workshop grounded in the real-world realities of cybersecurity.</p><p>​Participants will experience:</p><ul><li><p>​realistic cybersecurity leadership scenarios</p></li><li><p>​a proprietary leadership style assessment</p></li><li><p>​communication-under-pressure exercises</p></li><li><p>​burnout &amp\; stress awareness frameworks</p></li><li><p>​practical recovery and sustainable performance strategies</p></li><li><p>​facilitated peer discussion with other cybersecurity leaders</p></li></ul><p>​Pilot workshops are intentionally limited to a small cohort of participants to encourage meaningful discussion\, reflection\, and feedback that will help shape future Green Shoe Consulting workshops and the GROE learning platform.</p><p>​Ideal for:<br>Cybersecurity managers\, SOC leaders\, IR managers\, security engineering managers\, and team leads responsible for both operational performance and people leadership.</p><p>​4 CPE / CEU eligible hours.</p><p>​Cost: $350 per attendee</p> | Source: Chicago InfoSec Events Calendar | Tags: cyber\, cybersecurity\, health\, infosec\, security | https://calendar.google.com/calendar/ical/ChicagoInfoSecEvents@gmail.com/public/basic.ics
LOCATION:4225 Naperville Rd\, Lisle\, IL
URL:https://calendar.google.com/calendar/ical/ChicagoInfoSecEvents@gmail.com/public/basic.ics
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b94c2baa5addeeb8@zcyber-gtm.local
DTSTAMP:20260720T160039Z
DTSTART:20260723T180000Z
DTEND:20260723T200000Z
SUMMARY:Burbsec Northwest - Sponsors Welcome!
DESCRIPTION:BurbSec Chicago: The Midwest's Favorite Cybersecurity Events 🚀🔐 **Unlock the Excitement at Burbsec Northwest!** 🍻🎉 Are you ready for a night of geeking out\, making new friends\, and expanding your network in the world of infosec? Look no further—Burbsec Northwest is the place to be\, and everyone is welcome! We have **NO DUES\, NO PRESENTATIONS\, and NO PUSHY SALESPEOPLE OR RECRUITERS!** [Crystal Lake Brewing](http://crystallakebrew.com/)\, at the address below\, has a full bar\, but you will need to **BYO food** if you need dinner. 👥 **A Community Just Like You:** We're just like you\, and you'll fit right in! Whether you're passionate about infosec\, love indulging in memes\, enjoy a good beer\, or appreciate compliance jokes (among other things)\, we've got you covered. Our diverse skill set ranges from novice to expert\, and yes\, we even dabble in paper hat making! 🎩✨ 🤝 **Connections That Matter:** At Burbsec Northwest\, you'll find more than just like-minded people. You'll make valuable contacts\, form genuine friendships\, and expand your network of professional connections. These are the kinds of connections that come in handy when you're tackling that thorny problem at work\, at home\, or in the job market. 💡 **Knowledge Exchange:** Whether you're seeking answers to tough questions or ready to share your expertise\, there's always someone at Burbsec Northwest who's got your back. We thrive in a collaborative atmosphere where knowledge flows freely\, and camaraderie is key. 🕕 **Flexible Timing:** Don't worry about being fashionably late! People will start rolling in after work around 6 pm\, and we keep the vibe going until we're done (generally 2-3 hours) 🌐 **Stay Connected:** Don't miss out on the latest updates and community banter! Join the BurbSec Discord and follow us on Twitter for all the behind-the-scenes action and event sneak peeks. **Information Superhighway World Wide Web Presence:** BurbSec Discord: [https://discord.gg/4hhVPHebJX](https://discord.gg/4hhVPHebJX) Web: http://burbsec.com ([http://burbsec.com/](http://burbsec.com/)) Twitter: @burbsecnw ([https://www.twitter.com/burbsecnw](https://www.twitter.com/burbsecnw)) Mastodon: burbsecnw@infosec.exchange [(https://infosec.exchange/@burbsecnw](https://infosec.exchange/@burbsecnw)) | Source: BurbSec Chicago | Tags: compliance\, cyber\, cybersecurity\, infosec\, security | https://www.meetup.com/burbsec/events/315430393/
LOCATION:
URL:https://www.meetup.com/burbsec/events/315430393/
END:VEVENT
